    "turn_text": "not too bad. But my philosophy in life is, again, play offense. He better look out for me because I'm going to be on his rear end. He's got a lot of promises that he's made across this country that he has not done a damn thing about. You can go right down the list and I will. And I can start with my own hometown, which is why I think I'm best positioned to do this. because he made all kinds of probably came to our town and said, you know, we're going to bring manufacturing back. Don't sell your house. Literally came a couple years and said, don't sell your house. You know, we're going to get these housing prices back up. And since then we lost the second shift and then the first shift. And he doesn't do anything about it. No industrial policy to replace these jobs. Like I said, I don't blame him for everything. These problems were there before he got here. I do blame him for not carrying, carrying enough to fix them. Right. So I'm going to be at him. I'm going to be at carrier. Remember when he went to carrier right after the election in Indiana? Yeah. Well, now those jobs are in Mexico now. No one's talking about it. I'll be in carrier saying, hey, remember this? Foxcom in Wisconsin. Remember, he did this whole thing around. They were going to be him and Paul Ryan. They were doing this multi-billion dollar deal in Wisconsin is going to create thousands of jobs. That deal fell through. Right. I'm going to be in, I'm going to be there in that town saying, hey, remember he made this promise? Harley Davidson is shutting down operations in Wisconsin. I'll be there. I'm going to play offense. I'm not playing defense on this guy. He can call me whatever he wants.",
