    "turn_idx": 391,
    "turn_text": "Immigration, I think, again, this is a false choice that sometimes people force us to make. You can be for border security. You can be for making sure that people who are selling drugs or bad actors or terrorists don't get in the country. 90% of the drugs come in through the legal ports of entry. So that's where the wall thing, it's like you're going to put this wall in the middle of the Rio Grande River. That doesn't even make any sense. Let's just stop talking about that. Let's focus on the fentanyl coming in from the United States Postal Service. It comes in through the water. These drugs come in through legal ports. That's how we got to stop it. So you can be for that and be for a compassionate, economically viable immigration policy in the United States where you're not ripping babies from their mother's breasts and where you want to encourage people who are getting educated here and starting companies here to stay in the United States and create value and jobs in the United States.",
