    "turn_text": "all about disease and sick care and profiting off of disease. And then the pharmaceutical companies are in the middle saying, Jesus is great. Like you guys can all have your debate about health insurance. and figure out who's going to pay me. That's what the pharmaceutical come. Who wants me? You want the government to pay me? You want the companies to pay me? You want the patient to pay me out of pocket? I don't care, but I'm getting paid. That's got to change. The way you change that is we have the discussion about health insurance, which is the only discussion we're having now. I want to have a discussion about health. Right. We are not a healthy country. 75% of the money we spend today on a healthcare system goes for chronic diseases that are largely preventable. So if you're a",
